{"body":"## Summary\n\nFixes #20.\n\n- Require the applicable checks on the PR merge result. Run authenticated GitHub integration on Linux, macOS and Windows, and use a deterministic local image fixture to verify image download and opt-out.\n- Validate changesets against the base diff, exercise versioning and both lockfiles, and install and run the actual npm tarball before publishing.\n- Pin a supported npm publishing runtime, verify the package's trusted publisher before versioning, and verify the public registry version, latest tag and installed executable before creating the GitHub Release. An interrupted release can retry the same version commit.\n- Validate workflows, dependency locks, secrets, documentation and file limits. The evidence folder contains the historical logs, incident timeline, requirement-by-requirement analysis and a complete file-tree comparison with the JavaScript template.\n- Reported the shared distinction between an accepted npm OIDC exchange and direct publish authorization in [template issue #323](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/323).\n\n## Reproduction\n\n[Main run 37561736761](https://github.com/link-foundation/gh-load-issue/actions/runs/37561736761) accepted a failed npm upgrade on Node 20, continued on npm 10, and pushed version 0.4.0 before npm returned E404. [Placeholder run 45953561496](https://github.com/link-foundation/gh-load-issue/actions/runs/45953561496) incorrectly required a changeset for a placeholder-only edit and skipped downstream checks.\n\n[The earlier ready-for-review run](https://github.com/link-foundation/gh-load-issue/actions/runs/45956341596) timed out before Changesets reported a result. Version preparation now calls the installed CLI directly, updates the npm lock version without re-resolving dependencies, and emits separate, bounded phases.\n\n[Investigation and archived logs](https://github.com/link-foundation/gh-load-issue/tree/issue-20-4be44752c8ed/dev/log/issues/20/pulls/21)\n\n## Verification\n\n- `bun test tests/test-ci-release.test.mjs tests/test-npm-release.test.mjs` reproduces the runtime, authorization, changeset, required-gate and release errors with bounded fixtures.\n- `bash experiments/reproduce-release-recovery.sh` uses a disposable Git remote to exercise the real 0.4.1 version bump, fresh install, retry and recovery without registry writes.\n- [GitHub Actions on the current PR head](https://github.com/link-foundation/gh-load-issue/actions/runs/45957888107) passed 78 tests on each of Linux, macOS and Windows, installed the 0.4.1 npm tarball, and passed lint, workflow, lockfile, secret, documentation and required-result checks.\n\n- [Manual checks-only dispatch](https://github.com/link-foundation/gh-load-issue/actions/runs/45956811255) passed before the versioning follow-up and skipped the release jobs.\n\nProduction publication and GitHub Release creation run from trusted main only. The package's current trusted publisher settings are visible to npm package maintainers. A repository owner must configure `RELEASE_PR_TOKEN` to exercise the optional manual draft-Changeset PR workflow.\n","comments":[],"headRefOid":"91b994ccc45a9ccce1e5bc8b328de5f539a03319","isDraft":false,"latestReviews":[],"mergeStateStatus":"CLEAN","reviewDecision":"","reviewRequests":[],"state":"OPEN","title":"Fix CI checks and make npm releases verifiable","url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/gh-load-issue/pull/21"}
